    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias when the recent history shows a downward trend followed by a spike in sentiment (e.g., Example 1 and 2), failing to anticipate the subsequent volatility surge.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate price spikes that occur after a period of low sentiment (0.00) combined with a sharp drop in historical prices, indicating a lag in reacting to negative momentum reversal signals.",
    "The model displays excessive mean reversion bias, predicting smooth linear growth or decline while true outcomes show high-frequency oscillations and sudden reversals regardless of sentiment direction.",
    "When the last 3 days of history are below the forecasted path, the model fails to account for a 'mean reversion' spike that pushes prices significantly above the forecast trajectory within the first 10 days.",
    "Sentiment spikes (0.20) occurring after a price drop correlate with higher-than-forecast volatility; the model should apply a variance correction factor rather than a simple directional adjustment."
